amount for transfer</p>"},{"location":"api/models/#aiorocket2.models.Currency.min_cheque","title":"<code>min_cheque</code>  <code>instance-attribute</code>","text":"<p>Minimal amount for cheque</p>"},{"location":"api/models/#aiorocket2.models.Currency.min_invoice","title":"<code>min_invoice</code>  <code>instance-attribute</code>","text":"<p>Minimal amount for invoice</p>"},{"location":"api/models/#aiorocket2.models.Currency.min_withdraw","title":"<code>min_withdraw</code>  <code>instance-attribute</code>","text":"<p>Minimal amount for withdrawals</p>"},{"location":"api/models/#aiorocket2.models.Currency-functions","title":"Methods:","text":""},{"location":"api/models/#aiorocket2.models.Currency.from_api","title":"<code>from_api(j)</code>  <code>classmethod</code>","text":"<p>Build Currency from API JSON object.</p>"},{"location":"api/models/#aiorocket2.models-functions","title":"Functions:","text":""},{"location":"api/models/#aiorocket2.models.to_dict","title":"<code>to_dict(obj, keep_enums=False, keep_datetime=False)</code>","text":"<p>Recursively converts an object to a dictionary suitable for JSON serialization.</p> <p>Supports: - dataclass: recursively converts all fields. - Enum: returns the enum value if keep_enums=False, otherwise returns the Enum object. - list: recursively converts all elements. - dict: recursively converts all values. - datetime: returns ISO-formatted string if keep_datetime=False, otherwise returns the datetime object.</p> <p>Parameters:</p> Name Type Description Default <code>obj</code> <code>Any</code> <p>Any object to convert.</p> required <code>keep_enums</code> <code>bool</code> <p>If True, keeps Enum objects, otherwise returns their values.</p> <code>False</code> <code>keep_datetime</code> <code>bool</code> <p>If True, keeps datetime objects, otherwise returns ISO string.</p> <code>False</code> <p>Returns:</p> Name Type Description <code>dict</code> <code>dict</code> <p>recursively converted object.</p>"},{"location":"api/tags/","title":"Tags","text":""},{"location":"api/tags/#aiorocket2.tags","title":"<code>tags</code>","text":"<p>The API is splitted by tags. Here is the same splitting</p>"},{"location":"api/tags/#aiorocket2.tags-classes","title":"Classes","text":""},{"location":"api/tags/#aiorocket2.tags.Tags","title":"<code>Tags</code>","text":"<p>               Bases: <code>Version</code>, <code>App</code>, <code>MultiCheque</code>, <code>TgInvoices</code>, <code>WithdrawalLink</code>, <code>Currencies</code>, <code>Health</code></p> <p>General class to join all tags together</p>"},{"location":"api/utils/","title":"Utilities","text":""},{"location":"api/utils/#aiorocket2.utils","title":"<code>utils</code>","text":"<p>additional functions used by aiorocket2</p>"},{"location":"api/utils/#aiorocket2.utils-functions","title":"Functions:","text":""},{"location":"api/utils/#aiorocket2.utils.generate_idempotency_id","title":"<code>generate_idempotency_id()</code>","text":"<p>Generate a simple idempotency identifier based on the current timestamp.</p> <p>The xRocket Pay API accepts <code>transferId</code> / <code>withdrawalId</code> for idempotency.</p>"},{"location":"api/utils/#aiorocket2.utils.backoff_sleep","title":"<code>backoff_sleep(attempt, base)</code>  <code>async</code>","text":"<p>Sleep using exponential backoff for the given attempt number (0-based).</p>"}]}